{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the Room A archive row-snapshot optimization and capacity-refusal diagnostic at exact head 74e34d2e8d8ce31165ebdb0b3014f7f09131c602, tree 94079284cd2d74fcd2c7d061c2b736701910f419, on builder/archive-room-a-plan-refusal-20261025 (review request bda4b2ad, my promise 02c3b96c). This review binds child request ee84ee86 (promise 6b984b5d) to this one candidate as its local partial delivery; parent request 1aedd35b stays open for the hosted refusing charge and hosted progress, which this head does not claim. The head may land on Main c5b8e00c: the merge-base is 1f3feea2, Main differs only by the technical-debt note, and git merge-tree against c5b8e00c resolves without conflict, so gate 80453 at this head stands under the documents-only rule.\n\nRead order: the primary note first and in full, then the request, the child request and the builder's promise, then the production diff (archive-row.ts, archive-budget.ts, archive-adaptive.ts, archive-driver.ts, archive-bootstrap-cost.ts, archive-scout.ts, archive-window.ts), the eight test files, the seal map, and the surrounding code at the head (the driver's pass, the row validator, the frontier cost formulas, the Mark manifest in archive-build.ts, the public v2 manifest in packages/git). The worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-archive-room-a-plan-refusal-20261025 is clean at the head on its branch; 15 commits above 1f3feea2; 17 files, +657/-68; git diff --check is clean; check-commit-messages reports 15 checked, 0 flagged; the 17 artifact events at this head name exactly the 17 changed paths; the note has no Markdown links and the gate's citations step passed at this head.\n\nProduction correctness, from the code at the head:\n- Token custody. consumeArchivePlanningSnapshot (archive-row.ts) accepts only an object key held in the module-private WeakMap, whose record must hold the same SQL port object, the same planning row object and the same budget object; it deletes the record before returning, so a second use refuses; it calls budget.check(). A forged object, a spread copy of the token, a copied SQL port, a copied row and a foreign budget all refuse (archive-row.test.ts:163-205 witnesses each). Missing tokens are not an error: adaptiveArchivePass consumes only when the context carries the rowSnapshot key, and otherwise keeps the original 32 KiB/256 KiB debit and serialization (archive-build.test.ts fallback witness asserts that charge).\n- Eligibility and original budget. prepareCapacityDeferral issues a snapshot only when the caller's row is the owner's last parsed row object and the budget is the one that parsed it, and only when the custody price is below the duplicate it replaces. The price is 4,096 plus archiveFrontierSnapshotCost(s) plus archiveFrontierRowCompareCost(s), which is 6s + 8,288 metadata and 24s + 8,192 input work as the note states; the strict comparison with 32,768 and 262,144 means rows over 4,079 canonical bytes keep the original path.\n- Descriptor checks before field access. dataShape inspects own data descriptors of the owner's original objects (prototype, key set, data descriptors only) before any value is read; identity of at, repository, confirmed and through against the owner's retained references is checked; then the closed-schema validator runs again (it spends nothing when pending is null). The accessor, object-valued and oversized mutations in the test refuse with zero getter calls and no SQL call.\n- Exact canonical bytes. The row is canonicalized and must equal the owner's retained text and byte length exactly; a changed scalar value passes the descriptor checks and is caught here. The planning row is an independent parse of that retained text, frozen at the row, at, repository, confirmed and through; pending and stopped are null by construction, and the remaining fields are scalars, so every nested object is frozen.\n- Unchanged controls. ARCHIVE_BOUNDS, the per-unit prices, the wake and payload compare-and-set, the frontier validation, archive-build.ts and the recorded entry bytes are not in the diff. The 32 KiB/256 KiB debit is removed only on the snapshot path, and the custody price is spent before the snapshot exists.\n- Diagnostic. ArchiveBudget.capacityRefusal is a pure observation (no clock read, no debit; the budget test asserts both); it returns null for unknown keys, non-natural costs, unsafe sums and zero shortfall. Each refusing site attaches its own refusal (lookahead reserve, debit inside lookahead, window metadata and entry, finish quote, migration quote), and the planner adds the site name. Only a no-prefix capacity exit or a terminal debit reaches the pass log; a successful partial completion after exploratory refusals logs null because the driver reads capacityRefusal only from failed results. The driver's catch keeps a terminal planner debit when a later check() throws the same stopped budget and clears it for any other error. In gate 80453's Vitest log the diagnostic appears 14,820 times: 14,806 null, 13 scout-open and one finish-affordability refusal, matching the driver shortage witnesses.\n\nRecorded cost and pending compatibility, from the code: the native Mark manifest is the canonicalized inventory with cost: budget.admitted() (archive-build.ts:124 and :162), so a pass that takes the snapshot path records a different planning cost; the public v2 manifest written by manifestOfPass (packages/git/src/journal-v2-manifest.ts:76-86) holds v, through, parent, format, entries, retained, omitted, foreignSources, anchors and legacyAnchors and no cost, so a fixed selection's commit does not change; a different adaptive cutoff can. Pending rebuild (driver step \"rebuild\", rebuildArchivePass) reads storedSelection(mark.manifest) and never enters prepareCapacityDeferral or the adaptive planner, so no token is involved; the fallback witness confirms the original manifest is kept and the exact commit and objects are rebuilt.\n\nQualified evidence, verified: the audit manifest at /private/tmp/artroom-room-a-gate80453-independent-audit-20261025-v1 has SHA256 a75b7884… and its three payloads verify (receipt.json 0e4ab231…); every path digest in inputs.json matches the file on disk, including the gate's own /var/folders stage logs. The raw gate record at /private/tmp/artroom-room-a-gate-evidence-20261025-v1 has expectedHead 74e34d2e, expectedTree 94079284, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed true, exit 0, before.json identical to after.json; stdout shows all eight stages at exit 0, \"Tests 3580 passed | 3 skipped (3583)\", Node 42, Counting 55, and the typecheck log prints 40 tsc contexts. The two adopted seals reproduce from the maintained producer at the head (archive-driver.ts d44b3d5c…, archive-row.ts 1cb161a8…), and scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs passes 4 of 4 at the head in my own run. Control 34726's receipt records 8 passes and the intended failure at archive-row.test.ts:181 after removing only the budget conjunct, with production restored to 706a3b54; I read that receipt and did not rerun the control. The 58947 and 44389 audit receipts record their original failures as FAILED with the stated frames; I read them and did not rerun them. The Counting figure is Node evidence, as the request says. No browser or hosted check is claimed and none ran.\n\nNonblocking notes:\n- The new installed case \"Grow Room A shape\" builds a 37-commit history and drives two passes inside the ordinary gate. It witnesses bounded progress with an exact remainder, which the incident needs, but it is a scale case; measure its cost in the next gate and bring it under the PD-3 scale-case ruling with the other six.\n- The adaptive loop sets capacityLimited and capacityRefusal at six sites with the same two lines; one small helper would remove the repetition.\n- The note's opening paragraph quotes 44389's exploratory quote figures; they are from a failed run and are labeled as such. Fine as written.\n\nArchitecture: the row owner issues credit, the planner consumes it, the budget observes refusals and the driver logs them; each stays in its module. The eligibility rule is an honest price comparison rather than a flag, and the standalone path is unchanged for every caller without a token. The diagnostic is operation-owned: a refusal is attached where it happens, carries closed site and kind values, and null means no retained evidence.\n\nSecurity: no new authority is created. The token is an opaque frozen object bound to one SQL port, one row object and one budget; it transfers a byte count, not allowance, and a foreign budget refuses. The planning row is the owner's independent parse, frozen throughout; caller objects are inspected by descriptor before any read and anchored to the owner's retained canonical text. Caps, prices, fresh inventory, authority and privacy checks and recorded bytes are unchanged. The diagnostic exposes only cost numbers and enum names. The seal map changes only for the two owner files it names and the values reproduce.\n\nSimplification: the two-line helper above; nothing else.\n\nFindings: none blocking.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d5682f9b6a44cde443df8e0dc4336d4febe6e1d8","binding":"assigned","head":"74e34d2e8d8ce31165ebdb0b3014f7f09131c602","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:91447f87ed0af70dd2763bb79972178b74756b19\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c3b96c3147859b2afc38231be419702f479cfe\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6b984b5dff2efb77db073f13470a7826f3d04160\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2af7c9996c5d5cf646030198566bd9e188b7bad6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}